According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, global Airport Sleeping Pods Market was valued at USD 210 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 225 million in 2026, before growing to USD 380 million by 2034 at a CAGR of 6.3% during 2025–2034. Longer passenger layovers, demand for convenient rest facilities, and airport investment in premium passenger services are supporting market growth.

Airport sleeping pods are compact, private rest spaces installed within airport terminals. Depending on their design, they may include reclining seats or beds, charging ports, lighting controls, climate management, and sound-reduction features. Airports and service operators use them to improve passenger comfort while creating additional revenue opportunities from underutilized terminal space.

